# Wave W17-Z (Farewell Spring): fare turf — spring-meadow turf, still flecks: a bright clean spring green carrying sparse pale still flecks where the meadow holds its breath around the pool, the quietest green in Borea (design: a fourth lake the old maps leave off; the spring pool stands byte-preserved in this ground’s field, the shipped flowerfield banked in it entire). Farewell Spring’s own ground — split from its twin the Vernal Path by stillness entire (the lane sheds petals in motion; the Spring is the still water at its end) and from Route 214’s open meadow by hush: that grass is walked through, this is sat beside.
